From acc6ea1cba26cbf45f5a89ac25275a0920bd1b11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alberto Gallegos <alberto.gallegos.muro@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 18:28:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add XPU support to FBGEMM sparse ops tests

Add XPU device support to misc_ops_test.py and permute_sparse_features_test.py.
Includes support for permute_1D_sparse_data and permute_2D_sparse_data operators.
Also adds XPU support to cumsum_test.py for asynchronous_complete_cumsum,
asynchronous_exclusive_cumsum, and asynchronous_inclusive_cumsum operators.
Also adds XPU support to block_bucketize_test.py for the
block_bucketize_sparse_features and block_bucketize_sparse_features_inference
operators.

Add focused correctness tests for get_infos_metadata in
split_embeddings_utils_test.py and generate_vbe_metadata_test.py. Import
fbgemm_xpu to register the XPU implementation and compare accelerator dispatch
results against the CPU implementation through the shared device-agnostic
accelerator helpers.

Enable expand_into_jagged_permute_test.py on the current accelerator using the
shared accelerator_available/current_accelerator helpers and device-agnostic
tensor transfers.

Signed-off-by: Alberto Gallegos <alberto.gallegos.muro@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Felipe Leza Alvarez <felipe.leza.alvarez@intel.com>

Co-authored-by: Felipe Leza Alvarez <felipe.leza.alvarez@intel.com>
